The social and dream spend rows on audit-log now have a reader. The planning summary that every assessment and plan reads (the YOUR TRAJECTORY block from scripts/extract_trajectory.py) has a new section showing them. Committed as 46bad6ce.

What it shows on the live branch right now:
```
## Phase spend (audit-log phases/*/spend.jsonl, last 7 days)
- social: 1 run(s), $1.25 summed cost_usd.
- dream: no rows yet (phases/dream/spend.jsonl is not on audit-log).
Totals are a floor: sub-agent tokens are not counted (yoagent#173).
```

How it reports:
• Each phase is in one of three states, each worded differently and never turned into a number: rows (the run count and summed cost), no rows yet (the file isn't on the branch), or could not check … — NOT zero spend.
• A run that left no usage record counts as a run but is reported on its own line. It is never added as $0, so every total is a minimum.
• The 7-day window includes its edge: a row exactly 7 days old counts, one second older doesn't. A comment explains why.

Two departures from the plan:
• No extra fetch. Instead of its own git fetch + git show, it reads the audit-log copy that evolve.sh already checks out for this script. That avoids a second network call. Run by hand without that copy, it says could not check, like the other audit-log sections.
• The size cap went from 3072 to 3328 bytes. The block was already at its limit, and the new section (about 240 bytes) pushed the module-size warning's text off the end. With the higher cap, the cut falls at the same place as before.

Checks:
• The new self-tests use a real row copied byte-for-byte from the branch, and they pass.
• Positive control: breaking the cost sum made 5 tests fail by name. It was restored in the same command, with no marker left in the file.
• harness_logic.sh passed (272/0), and cargo build/test/clippy/fmt all passed.

Docs and the issue: ARCHITECTURE.md has a new entry and the corrected cap figure. I posted a status comment on #944 and left it open:
• Done: social and dream.
• Decided, left as is: daily_diary.sh. No workflow runs it, so whoever runs it by hand reads its spend report.
• Still open: synthesize.yml needs @yuanhao because the file is protected. The comment gives the exact change: YOYO_AUDIT: "1" plus a step that saves the spend row, copied from social.sh.
• Still open, upstream: sub-agent tokens (yoagent#173).
